#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&okular; is a &kde; universal document viewer based on the code of the &kpdf; "
"application. Although being based on &kpdf; code, &okular; has some unique "
"features such as overview mode, improved presentation support and annotation "
"support."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "Basic Usage"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid "Opening Files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:77
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To view any supported file in &okular;, select <menuchoice><guimenu>"
"File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Open... </guimenuitem></menuchoice>"
", choose a supported file in the dialogue and click <guibutton>Open</guibutton>"
". Your file should now be displayed in the main window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have already opened files in &okular; before, you can quickly access "
"them by selecting them in the <menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guisubmenu>"
"Open Recent</guisubmenu></menuchoice> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After having a file opened you probably want to read it and therefore navigate "
"through it. Go to the <link linkend=\"navigating\">next section</link> "
"to learn more about this."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:92
#, no-c-format
msgid "Navigating"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:93
#, no-c-format
msgid "This section describes how you can navigate through a document in &okular;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are multiple ways of scrolling the viewing area. One is to use the "
"<keycap>Up Arrow</keycap> and <keycap>Down Arrow</keycap> "
"keys. You may also use the scrollbar, your mousewheel or the <keycap>"
"Page Up</keycap> and <keycap>Page Down</keycap> keys."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:100
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Another way is to hold the &LMB; down at any place on the document while "
"dragging the mouse in the opposite direction of where you want to move. This "
"procedure only works if the Browse Tool is enabled, which you can select by "
"choosing <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guimenuitem>"
"Browse Tool </guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The navigation panel on the left side of the screen enables two more ways of "
"navigating through a document:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid "If you click on a page thumbnail the viewing area will be brought to that page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the document has a table of contents, clicking on a table of contents item "
"will bring the document to to the page linked to that item."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Some documents have links. In this case you can click on them and the view will "
"change to the page it links to. If the link is to a web page or some other "
"document the default &kde; handler for that format will be invoked."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Additionally, you may use the following functionality to quickly move to "
"specific places in the document:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can go to the first page of the document using <keycombo action=\"simul\">"
"&Ctrl;<keycap>Home</keycap></keycombo> or using <menuchoice> <guimenu>"
"Go</guimenu> <guimenuitem>First Page</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:147
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can go to the last page of the document using <keycombo action=\"simul\">"
"&Ctrl;<keycap>End</keycap></keycombo> or using <menuchoice> <guimenu>"
"Go</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Last Page</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:158
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can go to the next page of the document using <keycap>Space</keycap>"
", <keycap>Page Down</keycap>, the <guibutton>Next Page</guibutton> "
"Toolbar button or using <menuchoice> <guimenu>Go</guimenu> <guimenuitem>"
"Next Page</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:169
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can go to the previous page of the document using <keycap>Backspace</keycap>"
", <keycap>Page Up</keycap>, the <guibutton>Previous Page</guibutton> "
"Toolbar button or using <menuchoice> <guimenu>Go</guimenu> <guimenuitem>"
"Previous Page</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:182
#, no-c-format
msgid "Presentation Mode"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:183
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Presentation mode represents another way to view documents in &okular;. It "
"can be enabled in <menuchoice><guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>"
"Presentation</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. It shows the document on a page per "
"page basis. The pages are shown with zoom to page, that means all the page is "
"visible."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:191
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&PDF; documents can even specify that they are always opened in presentation "
"mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:195
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When in presentation mode, you have an helper bar located on the top of the "
"screen. Just move the mouse cursor to the top of the screen to make it appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To navigate between pages you may use the &LMB; (next page) and the &RMB; "
"(previous page), the mouse wheel, the arrow icons or the line edit in the top "
"bar, or the keys specified in the <link linkend=\"navigating\">Navigating</link> "
"section."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:206
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can exit presentation mode at any time by pressing the <keycap>ESC</keycap> "
"key or clicking the <guiicon>Quit</guiicon> icon in the top bar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:210
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can also draw on the current page with a pencil. Click on the <guilabel>"
"Toggle Drawing Mode</guilabel> icon in the top bar to enable or disable the "
"possibility of draw in the presentation mode. The drawings are cleared "
"automatically when switching to another page, or manually selecting the "
"<guilabel>Erase Drawings</guilabel> icon in the top bar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:216
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Presentation mode has some configuration options, you can find their "
"description at <link linkend=\"configpresentation\">Configuring &okular;</link>"
"."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:224
#, no-c-format
msgid "&okular; Advanced Features"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:226
#, no-c-format
msgid "Embedded Files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:227
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the current document has some files embedded in it, when you open it a "
"yellow bar will appear above the page view to notify you about the embedded "
"files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:232
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>The embedded files bar</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:238
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>The embedded files bar</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:242
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this case, you can either click on the link in the text of the bar or choose "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Embedded Files</guimenuitem>"
"</menuchoice> to open the embedded files dialog. The dialog allows you to view "
"the embedded files and to extract them."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:250
#, no-c-format
msgid "Annotations"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:251
#, no-c-format
msgid "&okular; allows you to review and annotate your documents."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:255
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Due to DRM limitations (typically with &PDF; documents), adding, editing some "
"properties or removing annotations could not be possible."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:261
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adding annotations"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:262
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To add some annotations to the document, you have to activate the annotating "
"toolbar. This is done by either selecting <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu>"
"<guimenuitem>Review</guimenuitem></menuchoice> or pressing <keycap>F6</keycap>"
". Once the annotating toolbar is shown, just press one of its buttons to start "
"constructing that annotation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:270
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The annotating toolbar can be docked in any side of the viewing are: just drag "
"it to move it to another place."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:276
#, no-c-format
msgid "Activating the annotating toolbar will make you switch to the Normal Mode."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:280
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can stop the construction any time by pressing again on the button of the "
"annotation you are constructing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:284
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The newly constructed annotation will have as author the author you set in the "
"<guilabel>Identity</guilabel> section in the <link linkend=\"configure\">"
"settings</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:291
#, no-c-format
msgid "Removing annotations"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:292
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To remove an annotation, just click on it with the &RMB;, and select "
"<guimenuitem>Remove</guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:296
#, no-c-format
msgid "When removing the annotation, its window will be closed if open."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:300
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This option could not be enabled because the document does not allow removing "
"annotations."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:307
#, no-c-format
msgid "Editing annotations"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:308
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To edit an annotation, click on it with the &RMB; and select <guimenuitem>"
"Properties...</guimenuitem>. A dialog will appear with the general annotation "
"settings (like color and opacity, author, &etc;) and the settings specific to "
"that annotation type."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:315
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Depending on the document permissions (typically with &PDF; documents), some "
"options can be disabled."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:325
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Menubar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:328
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenu>File</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:332
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>O</keycap></keycombo> "
"</shortcut> <guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Open...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:341
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Open</action> a supported file. If there is already an opened file it "
"will be closed. For more information, see the section about <link "
"linkend=\"opening\">Opening Files</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:350
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Open Recent</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:356
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Open</action> a file which was used previously from a submenu. If a "
"file is currently being displayed it will be closed. For more information, see "
"the section about <link linkend=\"opening\">Opening Files</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:367
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Save As...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:373
#, no-c-format
msgid "<action>Save</action> the currently open file under a different name."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:379
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>P</keycap></keycombo>"
"</shortcut> <guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Print...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:386
#, no-c-format
msgid "<action>Print</action> the currently displayed document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:394
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Print Preview...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:400
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Show a preview</action> of how the currently displayed document would "
"be printed with the default options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:409
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Properties</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:415
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Display some basic information</action> about the document, such as "
"title, author, creation date, and details about the fonts used. The available "
"information depends on the type of document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:422
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Embedded Files...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:428
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Show the files embedded</action> in the document, if the document has "
"any. For more information, see the section about the <link "
"linkend=\"embedded-files\">Embedded Files</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:436
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>Q</keycap></keycombo>"
"</shortcut> <guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Quit</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:443
#, no-c-format
msgid "<action>Close</action> &okular;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:450
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:454
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>F</keycap></keycombo>"
"</shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Find...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:461
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Show the find bar on the bottom of the viewing area that allows you to <action>"
"search for a string in the document</action>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:470
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycap>F3</keycap></shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>"
"Find Next</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:477
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Try to <action>find the previous searched string again</action> "
"in the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:484
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenu>View</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:488
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>P</keycap></keycombo>"
"</shortcut> <guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Presentation</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:495
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Activates</action> the Presentation Mode. For more information, see the "
"section about <link linkend=\"presentationMode\">Presentation Mode</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:501
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>+</keycap></keycombo>"
"</shortcut> <guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Zoom In</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:508
#, no-c-format
msgid "<action>Increase the magnification</action> of the document view."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:514
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>-</keycap></keycombo>"
"</shortcut> <guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Zoom Out</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:521
#, no-c-format
msgid "<action>Decrease the magnification</action> of the document view."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:526
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Fit Width</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:532
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Change the magnification</action> of the document view to a value that "
"makes the pages' width equal to the document view's width."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:539
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Fit Page</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:545
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Change the magnification</action> of the document view to a value that "
"makes at least one whole page visible."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:551
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Continuous</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:557
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Enable the continuous page mode</action>. In continuous mode, all pages "
"of the document are shown, and you can scroll through them without having to "
"use the <menuchoice><guimenu>Go</guimenu> <guimenuitem>"
"Previous Page</guimenuitem></menuchoice> and <menuchoice><guimenu>Go</guimenu>"
"<guimenuitem>Next Page</guimenuitem> </menuchoice> options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:567
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>View Mode</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:573
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This submenu makes you choose the view mode for the pages. The possible options "
"are: <guimenuitem>Single Page</guimenuitem> (only one page per row), "
"<guimenuitem>Facing Pages</guimenuitem> (two pages per row, in a book style) "
"and <guimenuitem>Overview</guimenuitem> (the number of columns is the one "
"specified in the <link linkend=\"configure\">&okular; settings</link>)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:582
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Orientation</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:588
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This submenu allows you to <action>changes the orientation</action> "
"of the pages of the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:593
#, no-c-format
msgid "The rotation is applied to the orientation of every page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:597
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can select <guimenuitem>Original Orientation</guimenuitem> "
"to restore the orientation of the document, discarding all the rotations "
"applied manually."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:606
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Page Size</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:612
#, no-c-format
msgid "<action>Changes the size of the pages</action> of the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:616
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This submenu is active only if the current type of document supports different "
"page sizes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:625
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Show/Hide Forms</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:631
#, no-c-format
msgid "<action>Show or hides the display</action> of the form fields of the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:636
#, no-c-format
msgid "This submenu is active only if the current document has form fields."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:647
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenu>Go</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:651
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycap>Backspace</keycap></shortcut> <guimenu>Go</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Previous Page</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:658
#, no-c-format
msgid "<action>View the previous page</action> of the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:663
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycap>Space</keycap></shortcut> <guimenu>Go</guimenu> <guimenuitem>"
"Next Page</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:670
#, no-c-format
msgid "<action>View the next page</action> of the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:675
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>Home</keycap></keycombo>"
"</shortcut> <guimenu>Go</guimenu> <guimenuitem>First Page</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:682
#, no-c-format
msgid "<action>Go to the first page</action> of the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:687
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>End</keycap></keycombo>"
"</shortcut> <guimenu>Go</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Last Page</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:694
#, no-c-format
msgid "<action>Go to the last page</action> of the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:699
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt;<keycap>Left</keycap></keycombo>"
"</shortcut> <guimenu>Go</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Back</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:706
#, no-c-format
msgid "<action>Go back to the previous view</action> of the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:711
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt;<keycap>Right</keycap></keycombo>"
"</shortcut> <guimenu>Go</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Forward</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:718
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Move forward to the next view</action> of the document. This only works "
"if you have already moved back before."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:723
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>G</keycap></keycombo>"
"</shortcut> <guimenu>Go</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Go to Page</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:730
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Open a dialog which allows you to <action>go to any page</action> "
"of the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:737
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenu>Bookmarks</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:741
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Bookmarks</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Add/Remove Bookmark</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:747
#, no-c-format
msgid "<action>Add or remove a bookmark for the current page</action>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:754
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Bookmarks</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Previous Bookmark</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:760
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Go to the previous bookmarked page</action>, or do nothing if there are "
"no bookmarked pages prior to the current one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:766
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Bookmarks</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Next Bookmark</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:772
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Go to the next bookmarked page</action>, or do nothing if there are no "
"bookmarked pages after the current one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:780
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenu>Tools</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:784
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>1</keycap></keycombo>"
"</shortcut> <guimenu>Tools</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Browse Tool</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:791
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The mouse will have its normal behaviour, &LMB; for dragging the document and "
"following links and &RMB; for adding bookmarks and fit to width."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:796
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>2</keycap></keycombo>"
"</shortcut> <guimenu>Tools</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Zoom Tool</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:803
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The mouse will work as a zoom tool. Clicking &LMB; and dragging will zoom the "
"view to the selected area, clicking &RMB; will bring the document back to the "
"previous zoom."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:808
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>3</keycap></keycombo>"
"</shortcut> <guimenu>Tools</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Select Tool</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:815
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The mouse will work as a select tool. In that mode clicking &LMB; and dragging "
"will give the option of copying the text/image of current the selected area to "
"the clipboard, speak a text or to save an image to a file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:820
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>4</keycap></keycombo>"
"</shortcut> <guimenu>Tools</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Text Selection "
"Tool</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:827
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The mouse will work as a text selection tool. In that mode clicking &LMB; and "
"dragging will give the option of selecting the text of the document. Then, just "
"click with the &RMB; to copy to the clipboard or speak the current selection."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:834
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo><keycap>F6</keycap></keycombo></shortcut> <guimenu>"
"Tools</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Review</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:841
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Open the review toolbar</action>. The review toolbar allows you to add "
"annotations on the document you are reading. For more information, please see "
"the section about <link linkend=\"annotations\">Annotations</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:850
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenu>Settings</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:854
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>M</keycap></keycombo>"
"</shortcut> <guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>"
"Show/Hide Menubar</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:861
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Toggle the Menubar display</action> on and off. Once hidden it can be "
"made visible using the &RMB; menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:867
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Show/Hide Toolbar</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:873
#, no-c-format
msgid "<action>Toggle the Toolbar display</action> on and off."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:878
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycap>F7</keycap></shortcut> <guimenu>Settings</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Show/Hide Navigation Panel</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:886
#, no-c-format
msgid "<action>Toggle the navigation panel</action> on and off."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:891
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>F</keycap></keycombo>"
"</shortcut> <guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>"
"Full Screen Mode</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:898
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>Enables the full screen mode</action>. Note that full screen mode is "
"different from <link linkend=\"presentationMode\">presentation mode</link> "
"insofar as the only peculiarity of full screen mode is that it hides the window "
"decorations, the menubar and the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:907
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure Shortcuts...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:913
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Opens a window that lets you <action>configure the keyboard shortcuts</action> "
"for many menu commands."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:919
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure Toolbars...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:925
#, no-c-format
msgid "Opens a window that lets you choose which icons are visible in the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:931
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure &okular;...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:937
#, no-c-format
msgid "Opens the <link linkend=\"configure\">Configure</link> window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:943
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure Backends...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:949
#, no-c-format
msgid "Opens the <link linkend=\"configure\">Backend Configuration</link> window."
msgstr ""

